educed pain-related behaviour in P2X<sub>3</sub>-deficient mice. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>407</volume>:<fpage>1011</fpage>&#x02013;1015.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11069181</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal">Cockayne, D.A., P.M. Dunn, Y. Zhong, W. Rong, S.G. Hamilton, G.E. Knight, H.Z. Ruan, B. Ma, P. Yip, P. Nunn, et al. <year>2005</year>. P2X2 knockout mice and P2X<sub>2</sub>/P2X<sub>3</sub> double knockout mice reveal a role for the P2X<sub>2</sub> receptor subunit in mediating multiple sensory effects of ATP. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>567</volume>:<fpage>621</fpage>&#x02013;639.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15961431</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Cordes, F.S., J.N. Bright, and M.S. Sansom. <year>2002</year>. Proline-induced distortions of transmembrane helices. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>323</volume>:<fpage>951</fpage>&#x02013;960.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12417206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Ding, S., and F. Sachs. <year>1999</year>. Single channel properties of P2X<sub>2</sub> purinoceptors. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>113</volume>:<fpage>695</fpage>&#x02013;720.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10228183</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Ding, S., and F. Sachs. <year>2000</year>. Inactivation of P2X<sub>2</sub> purinoceptors by divalent cations. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>522</volume>:<fpage>199</fpage>&#x02013;214.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10639098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Ding, S., L. Ingleby, C.A. Ahern, and R. Horn. <year>2005</year>. Investigating the putative glycine hinge in Shaker potassium channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>126</volume>:<fpage>213</fpage>&#x02013;226.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16103276</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="jour